  "description": "Non material amendments to planning permission reference: P/2026/01093/FUL dated 12th August 2026 for the \"External alterations to the roofs of the West Wing of the Tower and Lab Block including the partial replacement of failed roofing at 15th and 16th floor roof levels; installation of a structural steel frame platform at 15th floor roof level to accommodate one GRP enclosure to house two switch rooms and two steel enclosures to house UPS batteries; provision of cable containment at both 15th floor roof level and 16th floor plant room level, installation of an external riser to accommodate cabling routed along the building facade; replacement of existing glazed doors and windows on the west elevation at 15th floor level with new fire-rated windows and a solid door with a glazed panel, and infill of the remaining openings with brick.\"  Amendments sought are 1. Replacement window material: The planning decision notice appears to incorrectly identify the material of the replacement windows. The proposal is to replace the existing uPVC windows with metal-framed windows, in accordance with the submitted drawings. 2. Colour of the UPS battery enclosures: The decision notice describes the two UPS battery enclosures as having medium grey and dark red finishes. These colours reflect those shown on the drawings originally submitted with the application and the materials discussed in our correspondence up to 6 August 2026. \r\nHowever, the proposed colours of the two battery enclosures were subsequently revised. The updated colour for both enclosures is RAL 140 C 39 � Empire Green, to match the colour of the middle enclosure serving the switch room. 3. Metal ladder system and external cable containment: The metal ladder system and associated external cable containment, provided to support the electrical cables, have been extended to illustrate the full cable route towards the north across the roofs at 15th and 16th floor levels. 4. UPS 'B' battery room en